## Requirement brief
Marketing is launching a big campaign next week and will put our short links on billboards and
in a TV ad. Make the link service faster and more trustworthy before then.

## Amendments (these override earlier text)
- [amd_5305a8421c78] (product-owner): Update from marketing: campaign links must stop working automatically when the campaign ends (31 December, 23:59 UTC), and we need to see how many clicks each link got per hour during the TV ad slots.

## Clarification answers from the product owner
- Q-1: What are the measurable campaign targets: expected peak redirect requests per second or concurrent visitors, the redirect latency target (p95/p99), and the availability goal during the campaign window? -> ANSWER: Modest: up to about 50 RPS, p95 < 100 ms, best effort (one instance is enough)
- Q-2: Which database and topology will serve the campaign in production: SQLite on one instance, or PostgreSQL/MySQL with several workers or replicas? If PostgreSQL, should we pin a driver (e.g. psycopg) in requirements.txt? -> ANSWER: Keep the current SQLite backend and harden it (WAL, busy_timeout, configurable pool). Add no new driver. Document the move to PostgreSQL for multi-worker or campaign scale.

